==Old English==
===Etymology===
From Germanic ''*deuzom'', from Indo-European ''*dheusom''.

Germanic cognates include Old Saxon ''dior'' (Dutch ''[[dier]]''), Old High German ''[[tior]]'' (German ''[[Tier]]''), Old Norse ''[[dýr]]'' (Swedish ''[[djur]]''), Gothic [[𐌳𐌹𐌿𐍃]].  The IE root also led to Lithuanian ''dvēsti'', Lettish ''dvēsele'', Slavic ''*duša'' (Russian ''[[душа]]'').

